    "introduction": "Endeavour Mining produces gold from operations in West Africa, including mines in Senegal, Cote d'Ivoire and Burkina Faso. Its activities cover exploration, mine development, extraction and processing, with sales linked to the international gold market. Production volumes, ore grades and recovery rates determine how much gold can be sold, while energy, labour and maintenance affect costs. New projects and exploration help replace reserves as existing deposits are mined. Its regional focus creates operating expertise but also exposure to local security, government and infrastructure conditions. Reliable execution and disciplined investment are important because mine construction requires substantial spending before production generates revenue.",
